demy-id "q-48925" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|6x-4|}{3x+4}=$" :question/worked-solution "For sufficiently large negative values of $x,$ we have $|6x-4|=-(6x-4)=-6x+4.$ Consequently, for $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|6x-4|}{3x+4}={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-6x+4}{3x+4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{1}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-6x+4}{3x+4} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{-6x}{x}+\\frac{4}{x})}{(\\frac{3x}{x}+\\frac{4}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(-6+\\frac{4}{x})}{(3+\\frac{4}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6+0}{3+0} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48925/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48925"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3762/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "9b96f6db-9254-5076-a152-328b8b181782" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3762/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "543b94e1-01fe-5629-8725-915cbdb02bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3762/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "03f2e178-1832-5c45-8c83-767c50ff3816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3762/selection/ce613869d158ee65610d5a29cd642712ce8ff839e4d13681a91669926bfe6116" :answer/id #uuid "e668ad1c-25b1-5e4c-b042-4529e8390d74" :