fields ["q-3762/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698bf07"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3762"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339507/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "4b99e024-0827-5449-bdf4-75125c45a836" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339507/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "53891a93-adff-583b-ad1e-85c1380df81f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339507/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-339507/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339507" :question/id #uuid "000da502-b1b5-5116-a1b7-f93b9f904ead" :question/math-academy-id "q-339507" :question/problem "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|-12x+5|}{4x+3}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For large negative values of $x,$ we have $|-12x+5|=-12x+5.$ Consequently, for $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{|-12x+5|}{4x+3}=\\frac{-12x+5}{4x+3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{1}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-12x+5}{4x+3} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{-12x}{x}+\\frac{5}{x})}{(\\frac{4x}{x}+\\frac{3}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{(-12+\\frac{5}{x})}{(4+\\frac{3}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12+0}{4+0} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339507/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32cbf366-20bd-5a52-a14f-83add698b