emy-id "q-106694" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{2x-{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}+5}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{2x-{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}+5} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2})}{(1+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{0-{x}^{2}}{1-0} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106694/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "020c3de3-bcaf-5ade-ba50-2f15e344157d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106694"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339623/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "3ba531cc-1057-551f-9a86-2fc85ecd71b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339623/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "1336ebc1-00e8-5060-99c4-9d61efe3b6fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339623/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf039c6-d675-57a2-b9d8-6e8d13947e79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339623/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-339623/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" "q-339623/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339623" :question/id #uuid "a616dfb2-527b-5098-b8ce-2796ed00b6b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-339623" :question/problem "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}-2}{5{x}^{2}-1}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}-2}{5{x}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{({x}^{2}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})}{(5-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}-0}{5-0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339623/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "020c3de3-bcaf-5ade-ba50-2f15e344157d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339623"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339621/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "0f968f92-d46b-5506-b425-6806802a0fa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339621/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d360b2b0-6746-58ae-a7bd-df140cd0dc4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339621/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer-field/choices ["q-339621/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339621" :question/id #uuid "3bcb15bd-9c0c-5c65-97b9-07fcb59a2733" :question/math-academy-id "q-339621" :question/problem "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{9}-6{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{3}+10x}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{9}-6{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{3}+10x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{-{x}^{9}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{10x}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(-{x}^{6}-\\frac{6}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(1+\\frac{10}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\text{ }\\frac{-{x}^{6}-0+0}{1+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,-{x}^{6} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339621/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "020c3de3-bcaf-5ade-ba50-2f15e344157d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339621"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339629/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "08f099b6-c4d1-5d21-ac2a-c02d25a98fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339629/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "97633eac-78cb-5bea-bd54-88180978b6b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339629/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d88c5c2-353b-5e3c-9402-269cde16a082" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339629/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-339629/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-339629/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339629" :question/id #uuid "4bc264da-3bc4-5561-9fa9-e0a37b51fa53" :question/math-academy-id "q-339629" :question/problem "The horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{6{x}^{4}+6{x}^{2}-2}{2{x}^{4}+3}$ is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{4}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{6{x}^{4}+6{x}^{2}-2}{2{x}^{4}+3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{6{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(6+\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})}{(2+\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+0+0}{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339629/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339629"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35513/selection/f7031104f14fe004994e4fe4b8af3fbe4e65cfa2bff3c7eab1748f5f2092c758" :answer/id #uuid "ee46ed1b-b405-5a66-bc4a-3fe718d4890f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35513/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer/id #uuid "4073f650-a879-577e-a026-a773f80dda28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35513/selection/c3deb073f152a478e46392e1f56479f2987a022223419d7f9c369a815039d205" :answer/id #uuid "c8b5b82b-89ba-5989-bec7-2d9dcac1475b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35513/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "bf433b06-7dfb-52df-b2e4-e0ffaf91ca48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35513/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" :answer/id #uuid "0f94dc29-5f50-580c-9bdf-c64ab96fe471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35513/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9702e721-edd5-5b4d-8aba-b5576eb32250" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35513/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-35513/selection/f7031104f14fe004994e4fe4b8af3fbe4e65cfa2bff3c7eab1748f5f2092c758" "q-35513/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" "q-35513/selection/c3deb073f152a478e46392e1f56479f2987a022223419d7f9c369a815039d205" "q-35513/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-35513/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35513" :question/id #uuid "d425093e-9004-5661-b7d6-1c6b6cc8fb5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-35513" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{2-{x}^{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{4}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{x}{2-{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0-1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35513/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35513"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35763"] :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2x+5}{2{x}^{3}+2x+6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(2+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0}{2+0+0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339641/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "91924e9c-268a-549b-acdb-3bcd1759bd84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339641/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "94f42605-5fb1-5527-bedd-e379c95369fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339641/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-339641/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339641" :question/id #uuid "e6f0ac3c-98f9-5ddd-b191-1756531965cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-339641" :question/problem "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ for $x>0$ with $f(x)=\\frac{|3-8x|}{4x+1}?$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote is $y=$\n\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "For large positive values of $x,$ we have $|3-8x|=8x-3.$ Consequently, for $x\\to \\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{|3-8x|}{4x+1}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{8x-3}{4x+1}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x>0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{8x-3}{4x+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{8x}{x}-\\frac{3}{x})}{(\\frac{4x}{x}+\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(8-\\frac{3}{x})}{(4+\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-0}{4+0} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339641/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339641"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35831/selection/d4bb40b8e38dc5f1bae42b42e7394247fafb7a049afe6c9f70cb376abe30f139" :answer/id #uuid "c4084f72-1b9c-5365-8522-d0b138dc08fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35831/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer/id #uuid "c745edd4-05d9-53f7-abab-2c20c7db0f09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35831/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" :answer/id #uuid "8b3bc636-484d-5b85-96b3-0d5c42d00ece" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35831/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "bc2d79df-16bd-54f3-90e0-fae80e320a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35831/selection/c3deb073f152a478e46392e1f56479f2987a022223419d7f9c369a815039d205" :answer/id #uuid "852e1584-cf82-51dd-b11f-0e961c5afcb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35831/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "35ca9071-6662-5afe-ba8d-2d66e1d227d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35831/selection/d4bb40b8e38dc5f1bae42b42e7394247fafb7a049afe6c9f70cb376abe30f139" :answer-field/choices ["q-35831/selection/d4bb40b8e38dc5f1bae42b42e7394247fafb7a049afe6c9f70cb376abe30f139" "q-35831/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" "q-35831/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" "q-35831/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-35831/selection/c3deb073f152a478e46392e1f56479f2987a022223419d7f9c369a815039d205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35831" :question/id #uuid "89041eed-f9ba-5e78-85a0-a5586670c312" :question/math-academy-id "q-35831" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{6{x}^{3}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{6{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{6{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{14}{(6+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{6+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=\\frac{7}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78013/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "4e68efbf-9a54-5932-bd73-38c02dadc642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78013/selection/2e12ba8925bf524503f2444b8e9ba58bc68b822391e7a93f8ae4a9f7c858f0bb" :answer/id #uuid "1fd7aaa5-f065-54fe-aa19-b77d0d23be0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78013/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer/id #uuid "7179d099-ba6d-5ae7-a0d6-faac13f6c974" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78013/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" :answer/id #uuid "d27ad860-6d8c-58ad-b434-e6d399764bd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78013/selection/d5383cc560f7210ce951b287d42180f2c52a051d33d7310f4c07703ce1cd1b4e" :answer/id #uuid "a1776e98-0fb2-566f-acff-6ef5d0217776" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78013/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aeaf0918-d433-514c-9d30-7b9bfb23ef81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78013/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer-field/choices ["q-78013/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-78013/selection/2e12ba8925bf524503f2444b8e9ba58bc68b822391e7a93f8ae4a9f7c858f0bb" "q-78013/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" "q-78013/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" "q-78013/selection/d5383cc560f7210ce951b287d42180f2c52a051d33d7310f4c07703ce1cd1b4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78013" :question/id #uuid "bb18f206-4708-5566-8244-d67a975a9398" :question/math-academy-id "q-78013" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{4{x}^{2}+5}{2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{2}+5}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{x}+\\frac{5}{x})}{(\\frac{2x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(4x+\\frac{5}{x})}{2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(4x+0)}{2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }2x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78013/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bde258b7-1654-5e73-8703-0e42371db8f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78013"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101321/selection/0bb74c3f12c816a06e44c25108cd531b780e9c57982d2db5020eeef494c5d9d1" :answer/id #uuid "4ed9048f-464b-5582-9fb3-749f129d40ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\