tion/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{8{x}^{4}+x-2}{6x-5} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{8{x}^{4}}{x}+\\frac{x}{x}-\\frac{2}{x})}{(\\frac{6x}{x}-\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(8{x}^{3}+1-\\frac{2}{x})}{(6-\\frac{5}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(8{x}^{3}+1-0)}{(6-0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(8{x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-101321/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bde258b7-1654-5e73-8703-0e42371db8f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-68072/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer/id #uuid "36b5fef7-f91a-53f1-be44-a8476d359d4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68072/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "f9f8a9f0-2934-5bb2-acc1-705b289fcf96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68072/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "a314f518-cb1f-515f-bc4c-dcc6af849905" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68072/selection/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" :answer/id #uuid "d9df4097-1963-5b33-aadd-b4e266535f86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68072/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "aabbba00-c010-5552-8c1b-3bbd78777d5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-68072/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa861b8-d4c7-5b09-b7dd-c98a15b62ed1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-68072/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer-field/choices ["q-68072/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" "q-68072/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-68072/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-68072/selection/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" "q-68072/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-68072" :question/id #uuid "10717fa0-edd5-574c-b927-2b9585138eba" :question/math-academy-id "q-68072" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{-7{x}^{4}+3}{2{x}^{2}-4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-7{x}^{4}+3}{2{x}^{2}-4} \\\\  & {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{-7{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(-7{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}{(2-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-7{x}^{2}+0}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-68072/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bde258b7-1654-5e73-8703-0e42371db8f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-68072"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35834"] :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{12x-3{x}^{4}}{3{x}^{2}+7} \\\\  & {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{12x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{12}{x}-3{x}^{2})}{(3+\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{0-3{x}^{2}}{3+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-106702/selection/409e1ad0b502fc257eb8c830157d0bfd6ff84fc56d5849057f6e163524479b29" :answer/id #uuid "6d289c4d-66f9-5bc3-ba56-6f40a3dd4628" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106702/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer/id #uuid "eec3b875-66a9-5dff-878d-62bcc4f5aad1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptote" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106702/selection/66dee67ffc669624514ff5b1a417668a9eae11294f1a628debb8f62b82e75a0c" :answer/id #uuid "57140c10-c243-59a6-a36d-d4ee1187cf49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106702/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" :answer/id #uuid "938099ab-6674-5275-bf78-41bf3fd9fe1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106702/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "1fd6c2f5-fa61-51d4-8143-2a3ff0cb7e38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106702/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf9256b-03e8-5ac3-88fd-10615dd8ed9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106702/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" :answer-field/choices ["q-106702/selection/409e1ad0b502fc257eb8c830157d0bfd6ff84fc56d5849057f6e163524479b29" "q-106702/selection/b4433cc3a1cf5e75fc9a785442bb7c0d16a914e01f6e6fe624ef0ea36d614fe6" "q-106702/selection/66dee67ffc669624514ff5b1a417668a9eae11294f1a628debb8f62b82e75a0c" "q-106702/selection/dbaf85835946aefb97564ba0d1ea287b684a4c8821f4256502e349376df74d28" "q-106702/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106702" :question/id #uuid "062f25d0-e65b-58a6-96b7-d2cc83f47308" :question/math-academy-id "q-106702" :question/problem "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{11{x}^{5}-9{x}^{6}}{2{x}^{5}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{5}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{11{x}^{5}-9{x}^{6}}{2{x}^{5}-1} \\\\  & {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{11{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{9{x}^{6}}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(11-9x)}{(2-\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{11-9x}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(11-9x) \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106702/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bde258b7-1654-5e73-8703-0e42371db8f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106702"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
